+Actually, this might not be a problem.  If the option flag were there,
+it could be checked in both occasions: (1) when the game considers
+creating a bones level and (2) when it considers loading a bones
+level.  Someone with the 'bones' option disabled would never ever
+create or encounter a bones levels.  All other players would still
+merrily be using them.

Yes, but this would mean that the game would NOT be the same anymore
for the various players on our multi-player system. The opinions may
vary on which is the hardest to play: with or without bones levels. I's
say that playing with bones is easier, but I'm sure not everyone would
agree on this. Also, players could decide only to enable the bones
levels when there were lots of them, of course created by others. They
would use up some of these, and play their next games without setting
bones, thus having only a small chance of creating a bones level, and
having much greater chances of using up someone else's bones.

Summarized: I think one should only be able to set creating bones
levels at compile-time, but, to keep the game the same for everyone
playing, one should NOT be able to change "using" bones. Either
everyone uses them, or no-one (implying that no bones are created as
well).
